===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
===============================================================================

The MIT grant above covers the files written by the authors of this repository.
It does NOT cover the files listed below, which implement methods published by
others and remain subject to their own terms. If you redistribute this
repository, or reuse these files, check their terms first.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
taap.m, taap_bound.m
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
MATLAB port of the reference implementation of Targeted Accelerated Alternating
Projections by Bastien Massion and Estelle Massart (UCLouvain), released at

    https://github.com/bastmas6/taap

and described in "Grassmannian Frame Computation via Accelerated Alternating
Projections", SampTA 2025, https://openreview.net/pdf?id=vng6moOJ9L .

At the time of writing, that repository states no licence, so no permissions
are granted by its authors by default. These two files are included here only
so that the TAAP baseline of our comparison can be reproduced. Please cite the
authors' paper, and contact them regarding any reuse or redistribution beyond
that.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
getBound.m
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copyright (c) 2019 Bashar Tahir, Institute of Telecommunications, TU Wien
(bashar.tahir@tuwien.ac.at, www.nt.tuwien.ac.at). Implements the coherence
lower bound of B. Tahir, S. Schwarz and M. Rupp, "Constructing Grassmannian
Frames by an Iterative Collision-Based Packing", IEEE Signal Processing
Letters, 2019, DOI 10.1109/LSP.2019.2919391. The file carries the author's
copyright notice and no explicit licence; it is redistributed here unmodified
and with that notice intact.
